sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/approach/mutant-morphant-discrepancy-prediction--claude-opus-5-5--2> a prov:Plan, delphi:TestableHypothesis ;
    rdfs:label "Two-feature transcriptional-adaptation rule tested as a single hypothesis" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/mutant-morphant-discrepancy-prediction> ;
    dct:description "Instead of a flexible classifier, test the mechanism's own prediction as one pre-registered hypothesis with no tuning. From El-Brolosy et al. 2019 and Ma et al. 2019, transcriptional adaptation requires mutant mRNA decay (an NMD-triggering PTC allele) and upregulates genes sharing sequence similarity with the mutated gene. Rule: predict 'discrepant' iff (i) the phenotyped mutant allele is PTC-bearing and NMD-sensitive and (ii) a paralog with ≥ 50% nucleotide identity over the region of similarity exists. Predict 'concordant' otherwise, including promoter-less or whole-gene deletion alleles, which the mechanism predicts do not compensate. Compute the 2 × 2 contingency table against ZFIN-derived labels (same rule as approach 1), Fisher's exact test, and the odds ratio. Pre-registered: supports if OR ≥ 3 with a 95% CI lower bound > 1.5. A natural experiment within the data: genes with both a PTC allele and a promoter-less allele phenotyped, where the mechanism predicts discordance only for the PTC allele." ;

    delphi:proposedTest "Odds ratio for discrepancy given the two-feature mechanistic signature, and within-gene allele contrasts. A strong association, especially in within-gene contrasts, would turn transcriptional adaptation into a quantitative predictor; OR ≈ 1 would show it does not explain most discrepancies." ;
    delphi:context "Fails if: Too few genes have promoter-less or whole-gene-deletion alleles phenotyped (fewer than 15) for the within-gene contrast; and allele PTC annotation is missing for many ZFIN alleles." ;
    delphi:hypothesisType "approach/data-test" ;
    skos:note "Steps: 1. Pre-register the two-feature rule, identity threshold and statistics. 2. Annotate allele classes from ZFIN (PTC position relative to last exon junction; deletion type). 3. Compute paralog identities (Ensembl Compara plus nucleotide alignment of the similarity region). 4. Run Fisher's test; analyse the within-gene PTC versus promoter-less contrast separately." ;
    skos:note "Difficulty (proposer's estimate of completion within about a month of agent time): tractable" ;
    skos:note "Tool: zfin" ;
    skos:note "Tool: sequence-analysis" ;
    skos:note "Tool: data-test" ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch05-06> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2022-tame-19> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://zfin.org/downloads> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://rest.ensembl.org/> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-019-1064-z> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-019-1057-y> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/ee98025a1960b300fcc06aa2106f51118b60f565/problems/approaches/claude-opus-5-5.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/mutant-morphant-discrepancy-prediction> a delphi:Concept, schema:Question ;
    rdfs:label "Predict which genes show mutant-morphant discrepancies" .

  <https://zfin.org/downloads> dct:title "ZFIN data downloads" ;
    dct:description "Allele types and phenotypes" .
  <https://rest.ensembl.org/> dct:title "Ensembl REST API" ;
    dct:description "Paralog sequences and identities" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-019-1064-z> dct:title "Genetic compensation triggered by mutant mRNA degradation" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "El-Brolosy et al. 2019" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-019-1057-y> dct:title "PTC-bearing mRNA elicits a genetic compensation response via Upf3a and COMPASS components" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Ma et al. 2019, PTC-bearing mRNA elicits a genetic compensation response via Upf3a and COMPASS components" .
}

